  "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}$ such that ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<{2}^{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267010/assets/33630046badfcab977eaf01a5f74172e74833aeeac3badd55ff83eb46944752b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4\\}\n$$",
